The spectrum of the resulting non-Hermitian Liouvillian superoperator $\mathcal{L}$ is complex and symmetric about the negative real axis. As shown in Figs.~\ref{Fig_Sup3}(a)-(b), when $\chi=0$ and $\mu$ increases from zero, the spectral statistics of $\mathcal{L}$ undergo
