In Huang~{\it et al.}, it takes 1 minute to process 16,000 shadow circuits for each walker (roughly 10 unique measurement outcomes per circuit with 1024 shots, yielding 160,000 shadow measurements in total), so that the time per shadow measurement is $3.75\times 10^{-4}$~sec. Projecting this to a 16-qubit system (an 8-electron, 8-orbital active space) with big-$\mathcal{O}$ scaling as $\mathcal{O}(N_q^8)$, we 
