ency and 2D space) is multiplied by the 2D target object $x$, resulting in 1D bucket-sum data $y$ in the frequency domain. This operation is essentially a “hyperspectral” multiply-accumulate (MAC) process. The pre-recorded speckle patterns ($H$) and the measured bucket-sums ($y$) are then used to reconstruct the image by solving an inverse optimization problem.
