\section{Solutions to the auxiliary problem~(\ref{auxbuck}) and related calculations}
\label{techcompt}

We collect here some technical computations that are used in Section~\ref{genasympt}. For the reader's convenience, we recall the definition of the double factorial which will be used extensively in what follows:
\begin{equation*}
n!!=\left\{\begin{array}{l}
(-1)!!=1,\eqskip
\fr{n!}{(n-1)!!}.
\end{array}\right.
\end{equation*}
In particular we note that the double factorial differs from the (classical) factorial as $n!!$ is the product from $n$ down but with step 2: $n!!=n(n-2)(n-4)\cdots$.
We will also use the equivalent expressions
\begin{equation*}
%\label{doublefactorial}
\begin{array}{lll}
n!!=
\left\{\begin{array}{ll}
k!2^{k},& \text{if\ } n=2k,\eqskip
\fr{(2k)!}{k!2^k},&\text{if\ } n=2k-1,
\end{array}\right.
&
\mbox{and}
&
%\label{doublefactorial}
n!!=
\left\{\begin{array}{ll}
2^{n/2}\Gamma(n/2+1),& \text{if\ } n=2k,\eqskip
2^{n/2}\Gamma(n/2+1)\sqrt{2/\pi},&\text{if\ } n=2k-1.
\end{array}\right.
\end{array}
\end{equation*}


